     "retrieved": "2026-10-24",
     "licence": "BSD-2-Clause",
     "licenceSource": "Carried with the Center for Spatial Data Science distribution, which states Coleman’s BSD-2-Clause terms.",
     "note": "WHAT IS TAKEN FROM THIS WORK IS THE GEOMETRY, AND NOTHING ELSE. The 32 sub-district polygons are Koch and Denike’s, georeferenced from Snow’s Map 2 and modified by the Center for Spatial Data Science in QGIS. None of the paper’s method is used here: it is an empirical-Bayes evaluation and recalculation, and these workflows compute rates, a rate ratio and a two-by-two table and nothing Bayesian. None of its recalculated values is used either. The counts and populations in this example are transcribed from Snow’s own tables and verified against Coleman’s independent transcription — and Coleman (2024, Social Science & Medicine 344) argues that this paper altered the primary data and that its results are invalid. The citation records where the boundaries came from. It is not an endorsement of the analysis, and a reader who met the title alone could reasonably think otherwise."
    },
